      "text": "To determine the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke's trip, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total distance traveled by Rex's car.\n2. Determine the amount of gas used for the trip.\n3. Calculate the cost of the gas used.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total distance traveled.\nThe odometer reads 74,568 miles when Ryosuke picks up his friend and 74,592 miles when he drops his friend off at his house. The total distance traveled is:\n\\[ 74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the amount of gas used for the trip.\nRyosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon. Therefore, the amount of gas used for the trip is:\n\\[ \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate the cost of the gas used.\nThe price of one gallon of gas is $4.05. Therefore, the cost of the gas used is:\n\\[ \\frac{6}{7} \\times 4.05 = \\frac{24.30}{7} = 3.47142857 \\approx 3.47 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3.47} \\]",
